<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Depfa Bank Europe names new managing director.</title>
<headline>Depfa Bank Europe names new managing director.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Depfa Bank Europe said on Tuesday that it had appointed Dermot Cahillane as managing director with effect from July 7.</p>
<p>He takes over from Tony Burke who has resigned from the bank to pursue other interests in the financial sector, Depfa said in a statement.</p>
<p>Depfa Bank Europe was set up in July 1993 and operates out of Dublin's International Financial Services Centre, specialising in financing the public sector in Europe.</p>
<p>It reported a net profit before tax of 25.5 million marks in the six months to June 1997 against 15.3 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
